# QA verify (always on)

This rule is always on in this repo (`alwaysApply: true`). It is injected into every Agent chat in this workspace. Nathan does not type a trigger sentence. After you implement or change gameplay or content, you run QA yourself in the running Godot game through godot-mcp.

If this chat has no `godot_*` tools, stop after the code change and tell Nathan: Cursor Settings → MCP → enable **godot-mcp**, leave Godot Editor open on this project. Do not claim you tested in-game without those tools.

Read `design/QA-PRINCIPLES.md` and the matching checklist in `design/qa/CHECKLISTS.md`. Write the report from `design/qa/REPORT-TEMPLATE.md` to `design/qa/reports/YYYY-MM-DD-<feature>.md`.

## When it fires

Run QA in the same turn you change any of:

- items, monsters, ops, formulas, combat, targeting, spend
- tutorial steps
- draft mill / Weak–Tough–Deadly (never the word "Tier" on player screens)
- player-copy wiring (lookups, fallbacks, HUD/cues) — not the locked strings themselves
- unique art registration that players will see in a fight or mill

Skip QA when this turn was only: reading, answering, Paper Fight questions with no code, or a copy flag with no behavior change.

## How to run it

1. Pick the matching checklist (New Item, New Monster, Tutorial Step, Core Gameplay, Copy/UI).
2. Drive the **running game** with the Godot MCP testing tools (or `tools/qa/qa_probe.gd` via `godot_exec`). Developer Test is the fast setup.
3. Fill the report. Every pass needs evidence from the running game or a test script: screenshot path, log line, or `qa_probe` state dump. Do not claim pass from reading GDScript.
4. Fix failures. Re-test. Loop **up to 3 times**. If it still fails, stop and ask Nathan. Do not keep guessing.
5. Set shipped cards to `live` only after the matching checks pass.

## Testing tools are for testing only

Use satelliteoflove **godot-mcp** to: run/stop the game, inject input, screenshot, read editor logs, `godot_exec` setup, `godot_runtime_state` / `qa_probe.dump`.

Never use it to write, edit, or save GDScript, scenes, resources, or project settings. Code and scene changes go through normal file edits (`Write` / `StrReplace`).

## Hard rules (do not "fix" these by rewriting copy)

- Do not edit `data/player-copy.json` text or author-locked board/catalog fields. Flag copy problems in the report.
- Player screens never show the word **Tier**. They show Weak / Tough / Deadly.
- Combat always-checks: Attack vs Bleed are different; Block stops Attack (not Bleed); Dragon ignores Block and plays no Block SFX; Goblin takes no Attack damage (Defeat still works); Da Boot / Sledgehammer / Fangs are Defeat paths, not Slay-by-HP-to-0.
- `main.gd` stays small. New test helpers go in `tools/qa/` (excluded from the Web export).
